{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_20","type":"agent_message","text":"Selected responsibility: CSS selector construction for `Element` (`cssSelector` path building, unique-id resolution, component escaping).\n\nAdditional refactoring strategy used:\n1. Moved the CSS selector responsibility out of `Element` into the extracted collaborator layer (`ElementIdentityOps`) so `Element` no longer directly implements that method cluster.\n2. Kept public API compatibility: `Element.cssSelector()` is still available to callers via inheritance, with unchanged behavior.\n\nMethods moved/extracted:\n1. From `Element`:\n- `cssSelector()`\n- `uniqueIdSelector(...)`\n- `cssSelectorComponent()`\n2. Into `ElementIdentityOps`:\n- `public String cssSelector()`\n- private static helpers: `uniqueIdSelector(Element, Document)` and `cssSelectorComponent(Element)`\n\nHow `Element` was simplified:\n1. Removed one public method declaration and two private helper methods from `Element`.\n2. Reduced direct responsibility for selector generation; `Element` now focuses more on node structure/serialization while selector logic is in the identity/ops collaborator tier.\n\nFiles changed:\n1. [Element.java](/data/henrique/langchain_prototype/codex/data/repositories/jsoup/src/main/java/org/jsoup/nodes/Element.java)\n2. [ElementIdentityOps.java](/data/henrique/langchain_prototype/codex/data/repositories/jsoup/src/main/java/org/jsoup/nodes/ElementIdentityOps.java)\n\nValidation command executed:\n1. `mvn -q -Djapicmp.skip=true -Drat.skip=true -Dcheckstyle.skip=true -Dspotbugs.skip=true -Dpmd.skip=true -DskipITs clean verify`\n- Result: failed due to sandbox socket restrictions in integration tests (Netty server bind `Operation not permitted`), not due to compilation/refactoring errors.\n2. Targeted behavioral tests run:\n- `mvn -q -Dtest=org.jsoup.nodes.ElementTest,org.jsoup.select.QueryParserTest,org.jsoup.parser.TokenQueueTest test`\n- Result: passed.\n\nExpected impact on smell:\n1. `Element`